# I see my brother in Russian: ви́жу бра́та
subtitle: "Say I see my brother and I'm waiting for a friend in Russian: a living he takes the of-ending when he is the object, бра́та, кота́, Ива́на."
teaches: ["grammar/object-ending"]
thumb: "band \"Lesson 14 said later. It is later.\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"I work as a doctor in Russian: рабо́таю врачо́м","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/56-russian-instrumental.cast"}

## I see my brother in Russian: ви́жу бра́та
